{title: Not My Plate}
{subtitle: Daniel 1:3–20}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] | [C] | ×3

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Taken from Jerusalem, dropped in Ba[Bb]bylon
New name, new [F]tongue, they want the old me [C]gone
Kings table spread [Dm]with the richest wine and meat
Da[Bb]niel made up his mind, [F]that is food I won't eat
[C]Asked the chief offi[Dm]cial, give us ten days of greens
Water and [Bb]vegetables, then see [F]what it means
If we look [C]worse than the boys who [Dm]eat the king's food
Do what you want, [Bb]but give us ten days [F]to prove
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I'm in Baby[C]lon but I'm not of it [Bb]
They can change my name but they can't change my heart
I won't bow down, I won't be bought
In Babylon, I still belong to God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Ten days later, look at them, they shine
Healthier and stronger than the ones who drank the wine
God gave them knowledge, wisdom, every skill in a book
Daniel understood the visions and the dreams they took
The king put them to the test with every question he had
Ten times better than the magicians in his land
So when the world says blend in, take the easy road
Remember four young men who would not let go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I'm in Babylon but I'm not of it
They can change my name but they can't change my heart
I won't bow down, I won't be bought
In Babylon, I still belong to God
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
